                "senderName": "NWS Flagstaff AZ",
                "headline": "Flood Watch issued August 28 at 11:48PM MST until August 30 at 5:00AM MST by NWS Flagstaff AZ",
                "description": "* WHAT...Flash flooding caused by excessive rainfall is possible.\n\n* WHERE...Northern Gila County, Yavapai County, and Oak Creek and\nSycamore Canyons.\n\n* WHEN...From Saturday afternoon through late Saturday night.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flash flooding will be possible in creeks, normally dry\nwashes, and swimming holes, and over recently burned areas.\nLow-water crossings could also become flooded, which would create\ndeadly travel conditions.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Thunderstorms are expected to develop this afternoon and continue\nthrough much of the weekend. With deep monsoonal moisture in\nplace, any stronger storm will have the potential to produce\nheavy rainfall and cause flash flooding.\n- Additional information is available at weather.gov/flagstaff.",
